// Mistral Small 4 (Mistral AI) — Model configuration
// Source: https://huggingface.co/mistralai/Mistral-Small-4-119B-2603 (2026-03)
// Verified against the model card, chat_template.jinja and config.json.
//
// 119B MoE, model_type "mistral3" (vision + text encoder), text AND image input.
// The "-2603" suffix is Mistral's own release-date tag; the checkpoint that
// carries the published template and config is the -2603 repo, so that is the
// source of every value here.
//
// NOTE: These params work for ANY quantization variant (NVFP4, FP8, GGUF, etc.).
// Preset matching is substring-based, so a preset for the base model applies to
// any served variant whose id contains it. The user model entry keeps
// its exact server model id; the preset does not rename it.
//
// Reasoning depth (per-request parameter — NOT a chat_template_kwarg; this is
// how the card's own examples pass it):
//   - `reasoning_effort`: "high" | "none".
//     Card: "high" = deep step-by-step reasoning for complex problems; "none" =
//     fast, lightweight responses for everyday tasks. Undefined defaults to "none".
//   - Any other value raises `reasoning_effort must be either "none" or "high"`.
//     There is NO intermediate effort for this model — unlike Mistral Large 4,
//     which takes low/medium/high and cannot be switched off.
//
// Sampling (card): "Temperature: 0.7 for reasoning_effort="high". Temp between
// 0.0 and 0.7 for reasoning_effort="none" depending on task."
//   - "high" therefore pins temperature=0.7 (a single official number).
//   - "none" has only a RANGE and no official value, so this preset sets NO
//     sampling for it and leaves the served checkpoint's generation_config.json
//     in charge. Raise temperature there yourself if your task wants it.
//
// Token budgets: the card advertises a 256k context window (config.json reports
// 1,048,576). The ladder is sized for the card's advertised 256K: head 32,768
// leaves ~229K input. If you serve the full window, a longer output budget is
// reachable through the Output Length dropdown.
//
// To apply manually, merge "config" into an existing model entry.
// Keep that entry's id, server and actual server model ID unchanged.


{
  "presetVersion": 1,
  "match": ["Mistral-Small-4"],
  "meta": {
    "source": "https://huggingface.co/mistralai/Mistral-Small-4-119B-2603",
    "verified": "2026-11-10",
    "notes": "Mistral Small 4 (mistral3, vision, 256k card window). Per-request reasoning_effort is binary high|none (template rejects anything else). temperature=0.7 is official for high only; for none the card gives a 0.0-0.7 range, so sampling stays with the checkpoint."
  },
  "config": {
    "displayName": "Mistral Small 4",
    "family": "mistral3",
    "maxOutputTokens": [32768, 16384, 8192],
    "capabilities": {
      "toolCalling": true,
      "imageInput": true
    },
    "modelModes": {
      "high": {
        "reasoning_effort": "high",
        "temperature": 0.7
      },
      "none": {
        "reasoning_effort": "none"
      }
    },
    "defaultMode": "high"
  }
}
